---
description: Authz and secret hygiene for API routes and middleware
globs: src/app/api/**/*,src/middleware.*,src/lib/auth/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# API / auth security

- No hardcoded secrets, default passwords, or JWT secret fallbacks. Missing env → fail closed.
- User resources: authorize via session user id, never client-supplied email alone.
- Admin: verify JWT (signature + expiry + role) or Auth.js admin role — cookie presence is not auth.
- Sensitive routes (requests, upload, leads, payments, chat, cibil, profile): `requireUser` / `requireAdmin` in the same change that touches them.
- Never return OTP in JSON. Persist OTP with TTL — no `global.*` caches for auth.
- Uploads: auth + type/size limits. Payments: server-side amounts.
- Do not add prod-reachable debug/test DB or OTP harness endpoints.
